# Canary telemetry — persistent per-provider deployments, measured from INSIDE.
# Generated by canary/collect.py. Do not hand-edit.
# HELP akash_canary_reachable 1 if the provider served the canary's /metrics on its ingress at the last check. This is the customer-visible up/down.
# TYPE akash_canary_reachable gauge
akash_canary_reachable{provider="alphavps"} 1
akash_canary_reachable{provider="hetzner_hel"} 1
akash_canary_reachable{provider="onidc"} 1
# HELP akash_canary_restarts_total Container restarts observed via boot_id change within the SAME lease. Excludes lease replacements.
# TYPE akash_canary_restarts_total counter
akash_canary_restarts_total{provider="alphavps"} 33
akash_canary_restarts_total{provider="hetzner_hel"} 14
akash_canary_restarts_total{provider="onidc"} 30
# HELP akash_canary_lease_replacements_total Times the lease had to be recreated (dseq changed). Says NOTHING about whose fault it was — see akash_canary_lease_closures_total for the cause.
# TYPE akash_canary_lease_replacements_total counter
akash_canary_lease_replacements_total{provider="alphavps"} 17
akash_canary_lease_replacements_total{provider="hetzner_hel"} 18
akash_canary_lease_replacements_total{provider="onidc"} 17
# HELP akash_canary_lease_closures_total How the previous lease ENDED, by cause: provider=the provider closed the lease (MsgCloseBid); self=we closed it (MsgCloseDeployment from our own wallet); lapsed=escrow overdrawn, we underfunded it; open=still live on chain, we orphaned it; unknown=the chain could not be read.
# TYPE akash_canary_lease_closures_total counter
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="alphavps",cause="self"} 10
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="alphavps",cause="provider"} 0
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="alphavps",cause="lapsed"} 0
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="alphavps",cause="open"} 0
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="alphavps",cause="unknown"} 0
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="hetzner_hel",cause="self"} 11
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="hetzner_hel",cause="provider"} 0
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="hetzner_hel",cause="lapsed"} 0
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="hetzner_hel",cause="open"} 1
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="hetzner_hel",cause="unknown"} 0
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="onidc",cause="self"} 10
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="onidc",cause="provider"} 0
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="onidc",cause="lapsed"} 0
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="onidc",cause="open"} 0
akash_canary_lease_closures_total{provider="onidc",cause="unknown"} 0
# HELP akash_canary_lease_lifetime_hours How long the PREVIOUS lease lived, in hours, measured entirely on chain: start from the dseq (epoch ms, minted by the Console API), end from the header time of the block its escrow settled in. NOT derived from akash_canary_uptime_seconds -- that is only as fresh as the last successful scrape, so it is a LOWER BOUND, and reading it as a lifetime is wrong by up to the collection interval.
# TYPE akash_canary_lease_lifetime_hours gauge
akash_canary_lease_lifetime_hours{provider="alphavps"} 214.1597
akash_canary_lease_lifetime_hours{provider="hetzner_hel"} 0.0189
akash_canary_lease_lifetime_hours{provider="onidc"} 176.2390
